<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#FFFEFB</color>

    <!--
      ============================================================
      HANDYGO NATIVE SPLASH FALLBACK COLOUR - SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
      ============================================================
      This is the ONLY place the Android launch-screen colour is defined.
      Everything that needs it references @color/handygo_splash_background:

        * drawable/launch_background.xml          (pre-API 21)
        * drawable-v21/launch_background.xml      (API 21-30)
        * values-v31/styles.xml                   (Android 12+ splash API)
        * values-night/styles.xml                 (via the same drawables)

      WHY THIS VALUE: it matches the flat, near-white canvas that fills the
      middle and bottom of assets/images/background.png - the region the
      Flutter welcome screen shows behind the logo and the "Shuru karein"
      button. Keeping them equal is what removes the white/black flash
      between the native launch screen and the Flutter screen.

      The native launch screen deliberately shows this flat colour plus the
      centred logo rather than the full background artwork: the artwork is a
      fixed-aspect illustration and would crop differently from Flutter's
      BoxFit.cover on many devices, which would read as a visible jump.
      Brand identity comes from the logo and this colour; the full artwork
      appears the instant Flutter draws.

      WHEN THE FINAL HANDYGO PALETTE IS CHOSEN: change this one value (and
      the iOS counterpart - see ios/Runner/Base.lproj/LaunchScreen.storyboard
      and the README in ios/Runner/Assets.xcassets/LaunchImage.imageset/).
    -->
    <color name="handygo_splash_background">#FDFAF6</color>
</resources>
